From 86892d7aefcf747e4502e5aa1e740bc527e03ac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 19:00:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gpu_info: inventory AROS accelerators through HIDDs

AI_PHASE: chromium-headless-phase-3

AI_STATUS: complete

ROOT_CAUSE: ANGLE had no AROS GetSystemInfo implementation, while a PCI-only fallback would conflate physical display adapters with the graphics stack actually available to Chromium.

FIX_REASON: Query the Vulkan HIDD GPU registry first for accelerator identity, priority, and BDF; supplement it with claimed display-class PCI devices; leave Gallium selection at Hidd_Display surface creation where its contract belongs.

SCOPE: BUILD.gn; src/libGLESv2.gni; src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_aros.cpp

VALIDATION: filtered GN regeneration; ninja obj/third_party/angle/angle_gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_aros.o obj/third_party/angle/libangle_gpu_info_util.a; x86_64-aros-nm confirms angle::GetSystemInfo is defined.

RISK: medium; an unloaded Vulkan registry falls back to PCI inventory, while runtime provider ordering still needs native boot validation.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 BUILD.gn                              |   5 +
 src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_aros.cpp | 244 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/libGLESv2.gni                     |   3 +
 3 files changed, 252 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/gpu_info_util/SystemInfo_aros.cpp

